\begin_layout Problem
Suppose that each consumer 
\begin_inset Formula $i$
\end_inset

 voluntarily chooses to contribute an amount of labor 
\begin_inset Formula $v_{i}\geq0$
\end_inset

 toward the production of the public good 
\begin_inset Formula $y$
\end_inset

, with 
\begin_inset Formula $v_{i}<w_{i}$
\end_inset

.
 By definition, at a Nash equilibrium allocation, written 
\begin_inset Formula $(\bar{x}_{1},\bar{x}_{2},\bar{v}_{1},\bar{v}_{2},y)$
\end_inset

, each consumer 
\begin_inset Formula $i$
\end_inset

 maximizes 
\begin_inset Formula $u_{i}$
\end_inset

, treating 
\begin_inset Formula $v_{j}$
\end_inset

 as given (for 
\begin_inset Formula $j\neq i$
\end_inset

), and taking into acount the equality
